# party — speaking of an element to a companion, and playing the companion
#
# Every member of the party has their own token on the map, their own trees and their own noetic
# pool. Speaking is a symbol under an observed element: it costs the speaker a point, hangs what was
# said under the element, and plants the element on the listener's trees with those words as its
# root — the listener was told of it, and thinks about it from there. Speaking is not switching:
# the member played changes only when a token is clicked.
#
# --fill-party is what makes this reachable: recruiting a companion in play is a long approach. At
# seed 42 the party is filled with the hyena Brindletail, and the protagonist is Kenryc Greygate —
# both names are seed-stable. The header names the member played.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --fill-party --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --location-type test --location-id 0 --npc-static --start-area "Test Yard" --period noon

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60
advance 12 180

# The visit opens on the protagonist, with both tokens in the yard.
expect [KENRYC GREYGATE]
inspect party

# Something to speak of.
click observe "Test Bench"
choose childhood_memory
advance 12 180
expect-state noetic points=2/3

# Speak: the speech mark under the bench, then a speaking modus mentis. One companion is in reach,
# so nobody is asked whom.
regions
click speak "Test Bench"
choose friendship
advance 12 180
expect-state trees speech
expect-state noetic points=1/3
expect [KENRYC GREYGATE]

# The hyena has the bench on its own trees now, with its own full pool.
click member Brindletail
wait
expect [BRINDLETAIL]
expect-state trees "Test Bench"
expect-state noetic points=

# The companion thinks and acts for itself. The goal is pinned: a beast's action modus mentis
# refuses to examine, and the playground's draw over the goals moves whenever an earlier draw does.
strategy succeed
goal smell
click think "Test Bench"
choose birdsong
advance 12 180
click act 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180
expect SUCCESS
expect-verb smell

# The result closed, the companion is still the one played.
click continue
advance 12 180
expect [BRINDLETAIL]

# And back, by the protagonist's token: their trees are as they left them.
click member Kenryc
wait
expect [KENRYC GREYGATE]
expect-state trees speech
quit
